# Apixaban + 10 Acetone: XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# Analogous to the other Apixaban Explicit10 confined XTB2 MD runs
# (Apixaban/Water/MD, Apixaban/DMSO/MD/10, Apixaban/MeOH/MD/10,
#  Apixaban/Chloroform/MD/10, Apixaban/DMF/MD).
#
# Starting geometry: Apixaban (59 atoms) using the REAL r2SCAN-3c/
#   SMD(acetone)-optimized geometry (Apixaban_SMD_acetone_Opt_Freq_KeepDens.xyz,
#   converged, no imaginary frequency, E = -1542.154947 Eh) - not a
#   placeholder from another solvent, learning from the earlier DMF lesson.
#   10 Acetone molecules use the REAL r2SCAN-3c/SMD(acetone)-optimized
#   monomer geometry (Acetone/r2SCAN3c/Monomer_r2SCAN3c_SMD.xyz, converged,
#   E = -193.119405 Eh), each placed with its carbonyl O atom on the same
#   12-direction sphere-shell pattern used throughout this project, rotated
#   so the molecule's bulk (the two methyl groups) points radially outward.
#
# Apixaban centroid = (31.537, -19.865, -0.109); max atom-centroid distance
#   = 9.03 Ang (consistent with the other Apixaban Explicit10 builds).
# Acetone's own extent from its O reference atom = 3.10 Ang.
# 10 Acetone molecules placed at offset 12.78 Ang from Apixaban's centroid
#   (the standard offset used throughout this project for Apixaban-scale
#   builds).
# Cell Sphere radius set to 16.0 Ang.
# Checked: min Acetone-Apixaban atom distance = 4.16 Ang (no clash), max
#   atom distance from the sphere center = 15.53 Ang (safely inside the
#   16.0 Ang sphere). Total atom count = 159 (59 + 10x10), verified.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 31.537, -19.865, -0.109, 16.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Apixaban_10Acetone_XTB_preequil_confined.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

